    },
    {
      "id": "df7b6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36); font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "d8766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dc766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Students must earn a \"C-\" grade or higher in all courses required in the major. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Communication Studies is compatible with the B.A. in Communication Studies - General Communication concentration at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. Prior to acceptance as a Communication Studies major, students must complete a pre-major consisting of all required lower-division courses plus the upper-division survey course (COMS 100A) and upper-division research methodology course (COMS 100C). COMS 100A and COMS 100C must be taken at Sacramento State. All Communication Studies majors are required to complete at least one 3 unit public speaking course such as COMS 4 or a transfer equivalent. Public speaking courses taken to fulfill the CSU GE Area 1C Oral Communication requirement also fulfill this Department requirement. Communication Studies courses may only be repeated once for a grade change. Students who fail to achieve at least a \"C-\" in two attempts in a core course will be disqualified in majoring in Communication Studies. The department also offers a degree in Public Relations. See the \"Public Relations, BA\" major for additional information. For additional information, please visit: Department of Communication Studies .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students must earn a \"C-\" grade or higher in all courses required in the major. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Communication Studies is compatible with the B.A. in Communication Studies - General Communication concentration at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Prior to acceptance as a Communication Studies major, students must complete a pre-major consisting of all required lower-division courses plus the upper-division survey course (COMS 100A) and upper-division research methodology course (COMS 100C). COMS 100A and COMS 100C must be taken at Sacramento State.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">All Communication Studies majors are required to complete at least one 3 unit public speaking course such as COMS 4 or a transfer equivalent. Public speaking courses taken to fulfill the CSU GE Area 1C Oral Communication requirement also fulfill this Department requirement.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Communication Studies courses may only be repeated once for a grade change. Students who fail to achieve at least a \"C-\" in two attempts in a core course will be disqualified in majoring in Communication Studies.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The department also offers a degree in Public Relations. See the \"Public Relations, BA\" major for additional information.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/arts-letters/communication-studies/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Communication Studies</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
